From: TunaOS Mesa comparison lab
Subject: [PATCH] egl/device: supply the loader matching the selected swrast screen

Run 41234225393 mapped the candidate RPM's exact libgallium bytes and
crashed in drisw_init_screen at drisw.c:623 (loader->base.version).
MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=swrast selects DRI_SCREEN_SWRAST, but the
DRM-device path supplies image_loader_extensions without a SWRAST loader.
Reuse the software-pbuffer loader table when that screen type is selected;
keep image loaders for hardware, KMS swrast and kopper.

This supplements c9b298660774291478323c5ef148362d9b136c3b; it does not change
EGLDevice enumeration or LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE policy.

--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_device.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_device.c
@@ -290,7 +290,8 @@ device_probe_device(_EGLDisplay *disp)
 
    dri2_detect_swrast_kopper(disp);
 
-   dri2_dpy->loader_extensions = image_loader_extensions;
+   dri2_dpy->loader_extensions = dri2_dpy->swrast_not_kms
+      ? swrast_loader_extensions : image_loader_extensions;
    return true;
 
 err_name:
